A||||3||Nashco||AAHH!!  Where can I get some Koni's quickly?||||4||
Z||000000||Nashco||05-31-2001||04:45 PM||||I finally got the cash to order some Koni's for the front of my 88, and then I found out from the Fiero Store that they're out of stock, and backordered from Koni!<P>I was hoping to rebuild my front suspension two weekends from now, but I still need the front shocks.<P>Does anybody know where I can get some Koni's without waiting for Koni to catch up on backorders?  I may have to go for the KYB's, but I was hoping to do a full upgrade while I had everything apart.<P>Thanks for your help guys and gals, I'm going to have to make a quick final decision before tomorrow morning.<P>(And here I was...so happy to finally afford them...that's what I get for counting my chickens before the eggs hatched!)<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||4
Z||000001||Uaana||05-31-2001||05:22 PM||||Try shox.com or shockwarehouse.com<BR>shockwarehouse usually has lower prices.<BR>shox has faster customer service.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||05-31-2001||11:42 PM||||Bryce,<P>I use TrueChoice in Ohio. They are an authorized Koni dealer. I send struts there  for rebuilding. They may not be the cheapest but they know their stuff, have a big inventory and are easy to deal with. Truechoice.com. 1-800-388-8783.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||05-31-2001||11:49 PM||||Well, I solved my problem, and very quickly thanks to you Uaana!<P>I got an online quote from shox.com, but it didn't have a price for just fronts.  I called them up (caught them before closing, thanks to the time change between AL and CA) and it's 192 bucks total for the two front Konis, and three day UPS <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  This is actually cheaper AND faster than the Fiero Store.  Well...if things go as planned I'll have EVERYTHING I need before next weekend....I sure hope this goes smoothly (knock heavily on wood).  The total was only 182 if I didn't want the standard UPS ground (free shipping on Konis).<P>For anybody wondering, they had seemingly good customer service.  I live on the opposite end of the country from my bank account (school thing), and they even wanted to verify that it's really my bank account, not a fake.  Kind of a pain in the ass for me, but I'd rather they did scan for that than not.  They were real courteous about working it out the verification before shipping tomorrow.<P>Thanks for your help folks!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
